  "supervisor_assessment": "**SITUATION ASSESSMENT**  \nOn 2026\u201102\u201118 a critical disruption occurred in Tarn\u202fTaran, Punjab, India, affecting the major hub Port of Mundra. The incident is 587\u202fnm from the nearest port, threatens 90 vessels, and could raise freight rates by 25.92\u202f% for at\u2011risk commodities (fertilizers, agricultural, coal, chemicals, consumer goods). The disruption is projected to last 72\u202fhours, with a Goldstein Instability Score of \u201310.0 and an average negative news tone of \u20137.76.\n\n**IMMEDIATE ACTIONS**  \n1. Notify all affected shipping lines and cargo owners of the 72\u2011hour outage and potential rate increase.  \n2. Re\u2011allocate 90 vessels to alternative routes and ports to maintain service continuity.  \n3. Initiate inventory checks for the five at\u2011risk commodity categories to prevent stockouts.  \n4. Activate insurance and risk\u2011management protocols to cover freight rate hikes.  \n5. Monitor real\u2011time news feeds for any escalation or resolution updates.\n\n**AGENT DELEGATION**  \n- **Route Optimization Agent**: calculate optimal detours and identify alternate ports for the 90 vessels.  \n- **Inventory Agent**: assess current stock levels of fertilizers, agricultural, coal, chemicals, and consumer goods, and recommend buffer stock adjustments.  \n- **Financial Auditor Agent**: quantify the financial impact of the 25.92\u202f% freight rate increase and verify insurance coverage.  \n- **Supervisor Agent**: coordinate all agent outputs, ensure timely communication with stakeholders, and maintain overall incident status.\n\n**REROUTING RECOMMENDATION**  \nPreliminary alternate port: Port of Kandla, a major Indian hub, located approximately 1,200\u202fnm from Tarn\u202fTaran and capable of handling the affected commodity mix.\n\n**",
